'''{{lang|es|Caldillo de congrio}}''' (Spanish for [[cusk-eel]] [[Stock (food)|stock]]) is a [[Chile]]an fish soup. The dish is made of {{lang|es|congrio dorado}} ([[pink cusk-eel]]) or {{lang|es|congrio colorado}} (red [[cusk-eel]]),<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.chilenacocina.com/2013/09/caldillo-de-congrio.html|title=Caldillo de congrio |work=Cocina Chilena|access-date=2015-09-18|archive-date=2017-11-07|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171107002912/http://www.chilenacocina.com/2013/09/caldillo-de-congrio.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> cusk-eel species common in the [[Chilean Sea]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fishbase.se/summary/Genypterus-blacodes.html|title=Genypterus blacodes summary page|website=FishBase}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.fishbase.se/summary/Genypterus-chilensis.html|title=Genypterus chilensis summary page|website=FishBase}}</ref> The dish is made by boiling together fish heads, [[onion]], [[garlic]], [[coriander]], [[carrot]]s, and [[Black pepper|pepper]]. Once these are boiled, only the stock is used. Onion and garlic are fried together with chopped tomatoes. The vegetables are mixed then with the stock, cream, boiled [[potato]]es, and [[marinate]]d and boiled conger.

Chilean literature [[Nobel laureate]] [[Pablo Neruda]] wrote an [[ode]] to {{lang|es|caldillo de congrio}} called {{lang|es|Oda al Caldillo de Congrio}}. The [[Communist Party of Chile]] has a tradition of serving the Chilean press and media {{lang|es|caldillo de congrio}} at an annual event at which important announcements are made regarding the current year.<ref>[http://www.pcchile.cl/?p=6081 Intervención de Guillermo Teillier en caldillo de congrio 2013] {{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130119203755/http://www.pcchile.cl/?p=6081 |date=January 19, 2013 }}</ref>
